  "description": "TRACKLOCROSS (SO-EASY)People have been riding fixed gear bikes on unpaved surfaces for a long time. We've been calling it Tracklocross, but we certainly didn't invent it. Initially it was probably just called \"riding a bicycle.\" No matter what you call it, riding fixed gear bikes in the dirt is super fun.\nThe SO-EZ is our tracklocross specific frame, with a geometry designed for off road agility and sweet skids. The SO-EZ is a great way to add some extra tire volume to your fixed gear smashing and introduce some extra spice to your local trails. It's not less sketchy than riding with brakes and a freewheel, it's just a different way to ride. Free your mind and pedal, and then skid, and then keep pedaling. It's so easy.",
